# Walkthrough - Internationalization (i18n) & Multilingual Support

We have implemented a complete i18n system supporting **English**, **Hindi (हिन्दी)**, and **Bhojpuri (भोजपुरी)** with instant, persistent language switching.

## 1. Summary of Changes

1. **Language Context & Custom Hook (`LanguageContext.tsx`)**:
   - Built a lightweight, type-safe React context and `useTranslation()` hook.
   - Automatically initializes from and persists to `localStorage` (`setu_language`).
   - Updates `document.documentElement.lang` on language change.

2. **Language Switcher UI (`LanguageSwitcher.tsx`)**:
   - Integrated a sleek language selector dropdown into the main header and mobile drawer.
   - Displays native script labels (`English`, `हिन्दी`, `भोजपुरी`) with flags.

3. **Translation Dictionaries (`apps/web/src/locales/`)**:
   - [`en.ts`](file:///c:/Users/ayank/Downloads/download/SETU-1/apps/web/src/locales/en.ts): Complete master English string dictionary.
   - [`hi.ts`](file:///c:/Users/ayank/Downloads/download/SETU-1/apps/web/src/locales/hi.ts): Complete, accurate Hindi translations.
   - [`bho.ts`](file:///c:/Users/ayank/Downloads/download/SETU-1/apps/web/src/locales/bho.ts): Complete Bhojpuri translations, annotated with a note flagging `"REQUIRES NATIVE SPEAKER REVIEW BEFORE PRODUCTION DEPLOYMENT"`.

